SENTINEL The Lighthouse README
------------------------------

Welcome to a simple text adventure for the reZet80 SENTINEL!
It is based on "The Lighthouse of Doom" written by Steve Kemp in 2021 for
CP/M and the ZX Spectrum.
I have completely rewritten the game using my text adventure engine.
And I have made many simplifications, changes and additions and also adapted
it to the 16- and 40-character displays.
To start the game enter "LH" at the prompt and press ENTER.
The display reads "The Lighthouse". Press any key to begin.

The game is easy to play: Use "UP" or "U" and "DOWN" or "D" to get around.
Type "I" to view your inventory.
To find out where you are type "L" (look).
Otherwise, issue simple commands (verb and noun).
So for example enter "TAKE TORCH" or just "T T".
The descriptive text is short and the dictionary is very limited.
Most items are automatically dropped after you use them.
There are four ways to die, but only one way to win.
If you die, the game ends.
There is no time limit and no score.
Please feel encouraged to draw a map of the lighthouse for yourself.

Because only 16 characters can be displayed at the same time sentences have
to be split on several lines.
Keep pressing any key until the sentence is finished and you see the prompt.
Playing the adventure on a 40-character display is more fun.

From the original game:
GAME PLOT
You're inside a lighthouse (trapped? doesn't really matter I guess).
You see a boat on the horizon, heading your way.
But "oh no!", the lighthouse is dark.
The boat will surely crash if you don't turn on the main light.
The game is over, when you either fix the light, or find another solution.
If you do not achieve victory within a turn-limit the boat runs aground, and
death will consume you all. (It is a _very_ big boat!)

